&lt;p&gt;Northwest Association for Blind Athletes (NWABA) is celebrating 10 years of its Winter Ski &amp;amp; Snowboard Series with Mt. Hood Meadows and the Meadows Learning Center. The eight-week program, launching tomorrow, January 7, removes financial barriers for blind and visually impaired athletes by covering instruction, equipment, lift passes, and transportation, supporting 300+ athletes over the past decade with 30+ participants each season.&lt;/p&gt;

